== Dough ==

Add @masa harina{240%g} and @salt{¼%tsp} to a mixing bowl and combine. Then, add @warm water{330%g} and mix together using your hands.

Knead the dough to form a ball that's sticky enough to stay together, but not coming off on your hands. Keep rolling and pressing with your palm for a few minutes.

If the dough appears too crumbly, add a tbsp of water at a time until you are able to form a texture similar to play-dough. If it becomes too sticky, add in a little more masa harina.

== Rolling ==

Break off pieces of the dough to form small balls (about 40g each). Roll each piece of dough in between your palms until smooth. You should get about 14-16 tortillas out of this recipe.

== Tortilla press ==

If you have a #tortilla press{}, cut a zip lock bag into 2 pieces that will fit into the press (one for each side of the tortilla).

Open the press and place a ball of dough in the center on a piece of plastic. Place the other plastic piece on top and close the press down gently to form tortillas about 5 inches in diameter.

== Other techniques ==

If you don't have a tortilla press, place your ball of dough between 2 pieces of plastic on your counter. Press the tortilla down with the bottom of a baking dish or flat plate, then begin flattening it out with a #rolling pin{} until quite thin (about 5 inches in diameter).

If you don't have a rolling pin, continue pressing down with a hard, flat surface until your tortilla is the same size as the above methods.

== To cook ==

Preheat a seasoned #cast-iron skillet{} for ~{9-10%minutes} starting on low and working your way up to just over medium or medium-high. If using a regular frying pan, preheat it with no oil as you normally would.

Add a tortilla and cook on the first side for ~{40-50%seconds}. Flip and cook for another ~{30-60%seconds}, or until brown spots are forming.

Remove the tortilla from the heat and wrap in a tea towel to keep warm while you cook the rest.

Serve warm with your favorite meals.
